 "confidence": "high", "notes": ["No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings.", "Open seat: Dick Durbin (D) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Dick Durbin's retirement opens a Democratic-held Senate seat in a state that leans about six points Democratic, and the 2026 environment adds further Democratic tailwind. Lieutenant Governor Juliana Stratton enters the general election as the clear favorite, having raised nearly $6 million and drawn roughly $9 million in outside support, though she also faces about $10 million in outside opposition. Republican Don Tracy has raised about $2.5 million and has run a Trump-aligned campaign that fits poorly with Illinois' electorate.\n\nNo public general-election polls are available, so the outlook rests on fundamentals, expert ratings, and markets. All ten expert raters place the race in the Safe or Solid Democratic column, and prediction markets uniformly price Stratton at 98%. An open seat adds some uncertainty, but the evidence points to a comfortable Democratic hold.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.9877, "margin": 15.07}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9857, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.9943, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9883, "margin": 15.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9819, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9928, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9849, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9898, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9888, "margin": 16.0}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9865, "margin": 15.0}]}